Found by k363 (9e13d5a, 2026-11-03). Nothing here was converted, because it was not on the card.

1. **Root cause.** OCP::Cmd::Apply::K8s read_or_absent, read_or_why and crd_get flatten a Kubernetes::REST::APIError into "could not read X: $reason". The reason keeps its " at FILE line N." location. After that, no caller can use OCP::ErrorLine user_line/api_error_line on it.
2. **Same class in CR.pm, not in the k356 list:**
   - _say_robocop_image_change: "[WARN] robocop image ..., not compared with the running one: $err"
   - wait_robocop_ready: "[WARN] robocop not seen ready: $why"
   Both print the read reason raw, location included.
3. **lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/Drift.pm prints raw $@ in its [!!] lines** (line numbers as of 895a9bf):
   - the remedy failure ~:250
   - Registry ~:291
   - GPU Operator ~:364
   - cert-manager ~:413
   - Cilium Gateway ~:434
   - "Could not list OCPNodes" ~:542 and ~:728
   - worker labels/taints ~:741
4. **OCP.pm _clean_message.** A user error that wraps an inner croak with "$@\n" ends in "line N.\n\n". `\s*\z` matches that, so the renderer calls the error internal. This is the renderer's own rule (ADR 0031): decide there, not per site.
5. **Init _ensure_age_key, both sites.** They strip only a location at the very end. A location inside OCP::Secrets' multi-line refusal would stay. None has been seen, because Secrets dies with "\n". Watch for it if 1 changes.

Done =
- read_or_absent/read_or_why/crd_get keep the error object, or a one_line-clean reason, so callers can render it;
- the sites in 2 and 3 print without a Perl location (test: a fake APIError with a location, then assert STDERR has no " line N.");
- 4 is decided in OCP.pm.

From k395 (8243616): OCP::ErrorLine::one_line now keeps only the first body line of a 599 Kubernetes::REST::APIError object, so the reason of an unanswering API is said once. A 599 already flattened into a string (read_or_absent/read_or_why/crd_get today) is not shortened: keeping the object here, item 1, also fixes that.

